  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan\u2061x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- $tan\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan\u2061(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan\u2061x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan\u2061x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan\u2061(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
